.policy "ruff-fix002-line-contains-todo" revision 3
.description "Resolve the missing feature, optimization or refactoring a TODO comment marks before shipping, then remove the comment."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff FIX002 (flake8-fixme): a comment whose first task directive across its `#`-separated segments is `TODO`,
// in any case. A directive is the first Unicode-alphanumeric word after a `#`; another task tag first wins.
// Reported at the comment; Ruff reports at the tag, on the same line.
//   # TODO: something           ← FIX002
//   # a # todo                  ← FIX002: after another `#`
//   # FIXME # TODO              not reported: FIXME is the first task directive
//   # TODOS                     not reported: not the whole word
.violation FIX002(at: node, d: symbol) code "FIX002"
    "Do the work this `{d}` comment describes, then remove the `{d}` note; if the work belongs in a separate change or the note documents planned work on purpose, leave it."
    suppress ruff "FIX002"
FIX002(c, d) :- kind(c, "comment"), text(c, s),
    match("(?<pre>[\\s\\S]*?#[#\\s]*)(?<d>[tT][oO][dD][oO]|[fF][iI][xX][mM][eE]|[xX][xX][xX]|[hH][aA][cC][kK])(?<rest>(?:[^\\p{Alphabetic}\\p{N}][\\s\\S]*)?)", s),
    match("[tT][oO][dD][oO]", d).
